Subject: [SE3-P4] wmvcore: pace asynchronous delivery from the start position

When the async WM reader paces delivery itself (no user-provided clock, as
qasf's WM ASF Reader uses it under a graph clock), it compared each
sample's stream time with the time elapsed since the reader started. After
a start or seek to position P it therefore waited P seconds before
delivering the first sample: a seek to 5 s showed nothing for 5 s, and
DirectShow playback after a mid-file seek appeared frozen or skipped. The
clock starts at the start position; add it. Playback from 0 is unchanged.

---
diff --git a/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c b/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c
--- a/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/wmvcore/async_reader.c
@@ -265,7 +265,8 @@
 
     if (!reader->user_clock)
     {
-        current_time = get_current_time(reader) - reader->clock_start;
+        /* Sample times are stream times; the clock starts at the start position. */
+        current_time = get_current_time(reader) - reader->clock_start + reader->active_start;
         timeout = (pts - current_time) / 10000;
     }
 
